  <ym-title|Trace calibration and scale-gallery producer
  audit><label|trace-calibration-and-scale-gallery-producer-audit>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Unit: YM-000026, selected trace producer.

    <item>Status: draft; local review requested, not whole-proof approval.

    <item>Imported Lean revision: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>
    (<verbatim|source/upstream.json>).

    <item>Manuscript: <verbatim|manuscript/existence/trace-calibration-producer.tex>.

    <item>Scope: finite-dimensional conserved-kernel rank, two-direction
    Ward-flux calibration, physical stress normalization, and recursive
    selection of a strict scale subsequence. It records the exact public
    caller and selected source producers. Funding and finite-volume chart
    receipts remain upstream inputs from the selected run.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Source correspondence><label|source-correspondence>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Manuscript
  statement>>|<cell|<strong|Exact declaration and source
  path>>|<cell|<strong|Correspondence and status>>>|<row|<cell|Reference
  conserved kernel is one-dimensional>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Further.PhysicalPeriodLimitF933.free_rank>
  and <verbatim|.free_closure>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/Further/PHYSICAL_PERIOD_LIMIT_F933/FreeRanks.lean>;
  <verbatim|YM.StressFlux.divergence_tests>, <verbatim|.div_kernel>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Push/STRESS_FLUX/FreeTests.lean>;
  <verbatim|YM.StressFlux.dim_free_five>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Push/STRESS_FLUX/Lift.lean>;
  <verbatim|YM.StressFlux.finrank_one>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/Push/STRESS_FLUX/Counts.lean>>|<cell|The
  complete free calculation is now stated in <verbatim|trace-free-rank.tex>,
  Proposition <verbatim|prop:ex-trace-free-closure-rank>: the low-grade
  coefficient classification gives raw bounds four and three; the one-point
  scalar and three Wick probes establish the stress coefficient isomorphism;
  the two differentiated probes are <verbatim|(-256,-512,128)> and
  <verbatim|(0,-512,-128)>; the nonzero equation-of-motion vector is killed
  in the Maxwell quotient; the probe functionals identify the two-dimensional
  quotient; and their common zero-skim kernel is exactly the Weyl line. The
  source crosswalk is recorded in <verbatim|trace-free-rank-evidence.md>. The
  source <verbatim|from_skim>, <verbatim|toeKer>, and <verbatim|toe_surj> in
  <verbatim|.free_rank> identify this reference result with the centered
  divergence kernel.>>|<row|<cell|Optical comparison has the same kernel as
  interacting divergence>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Shelves.Optics_pay> and
  <verbatim|.aprilA>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Shelves/Lore.lean>;
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Shelves.Hero>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Shelves/Route.lean>;
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Shelves.DSeed_pay>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Shelves/Sapphire.lean>;
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Over.cornel>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Chart/Stage.lean>>|<cell|The
  actual grade-five map is positive crown normalization times the inverse
  chart map composed with <verbatim|DSeed>; <verbatim|DSeed> is the
  divergence rank map. <verbatim|.aprilA> proves its kernel is the divergence
  kernel, using eventual coherent chart invertibility and positivity.
  <verbatim|.cornel> identifies this with conservation.>>|<row|<cell|Equality
  of dimensions of reference and interacting tensor
  domains>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Next.UVStress.centerEquiv>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/UV_STRESS/Dimension.lean>;
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Over.ranking>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Chart/Masts.lean>>|<cell|The
  manuscript gives the map: transform each tensor entry through the coherent
  grade-four field equivalence, then center it. The inverse uses the inverse
  coherent map and centering. Source <verbatim|transformed_mem>,
  <verbatim|enters>, <verbatim|locks>, and <verbatim|embrace> prove
  well-definedness and both composites, using unit
  preservation.>>|<row|<cell|Surjectivity of the optical map from two
  correction directions>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Over.pollen> and
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Over.formulate>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Chart/Laurel.lean>;
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Over.ranking>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Chart/Masts.lean>>|<cell|The
  two directions are the true and false pace directions. The composite from
  the two-dimensional coefficient space is eventually bijective by stable
  inversion; hence the optical map is onto.>>|<row|<cell|Stable inverse for
  the two correction directions>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Over.wend>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Chart/Limits.lean>; applied in
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Over.formulate>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Chart/Laurel.lean>>|<cell|Source
  convergence is pointwise on a finite-dimensional coefficient space and
  therefore operator-norm convergence. The manuscript supplies the standard
  minimum-on-the-unit-sphere proof and the resulting uniform inverse
  bound.>>|<row|<cell|Weighted bounded receiver from a rank-one approximate
  kernel>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.plumage>, <verbatim|.spend>,
  <verbatim|.expenses>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Delta.lean>;
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.springs>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Lease.lean>;
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Slate.rungs>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Slate/Garnet.lean>>|<cell|The
  manuscript proof decomposes <verbatim|y=Uf(y)+A(y)x>, sets
  <verbatim|V_i=u_i f+A\<varotimes\>w_i>, computes the weighted defect after
  evaluation on <verbatim|V_i y>, and composes with <verbatim|V_i^{-1}>. The
  source <verbatim|springs> applies this using the chart right inverse and
  two weighted vanishing estimates. <verbatim|rungs> supplies those via
  <verbatim|aspiring> and <verbatim|legacy>; those estimates remain upstream
  here.>>|<row|<cell|Correction size and exact
  cancellation>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Over.sizeQ'> and
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Over.formulate>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Chart/Dray.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Chart/Laurel.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|sizeQ'>
  bounds the uncorrected optical divergence by a constant times
  <verbatim|RQ>; <verbatim|formulate> gives the exact cancellation and
  coefficient bound by <verbatim|RQ>. <verbatim|YM.Trace.Over.river_k>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Chart/Dray.lean>, gives <verbatim|RQ
  \<leq\> taxA>. These are the manuscript's (A_ile a_i) and
  (>>|<row|<cell|Flux of uncorrected term and weighted errors of correction
  directions>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Over.transferX> and
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Over.mere>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Chart/Dray.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Chart/Token.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|transferX>
  gives the unweighted flux limit (-G.slopeConstant). <verbatim|mere> gives
  the <verbatim|taxA>-weighted limits: the false direction has flux tending
  to (0), and the true direction has flux tending to (-4). Combined with the
  coefficient bound, these imply the (o(1)) terms used to obtain (c_i^1
  o-G.slopeConstant/4).>>|<row|<cell|Conserved corrected sequence and two
  limits>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Over.serene>, <verbatim|.yields>, and
  <verbatim|.blossoms>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Chart/Stage.lean>;
  assembled in <verbatim|YM.Trace.Over.reveals>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Chart/Masts.lean>>|<cell|These give
  eventual conservation, the normalized tensor limit, and the trace limit.
  The manuscript rewrites their coefficient argument and records the
  equations in ordinary notation.>>|<row|<cell|Physical stress has the
  reference normalization>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Over.awake_o> and
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Over.year_spec>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Chart/North.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|awake_o>
  supplies a nonzero reference derivative observed by a Ward functional.
  <verbatim|year_spec> uses the physical and reference translation-flux
  identities, the one-dimensional conserved space, and convergence of the
  separated shell-flux test to force the scalar multiple to tend to one. The
  manuscript spells out this scalar normalization.>>|<row|<cell|One-level
  finite-volume selection>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.East.boatsSky>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Prom/Zoom/Boats.lean>>|<cell|Given
  <verbatim|FiresSky> at level (d), any lower index (Y), positive null
  sequence (s), and ( heta\<gtr\>0), the source finds (kge Y) with
  (s_k\<less\> heta), plus a finite chart whose radius is (s_k) and whose
  receipts hold at a level index (ige Y). The recursion in the manuscript
  chooses (Y) above the previous selected index and the
  level.>>|<row|<cell|Strictly decreasing sequence and increasing finite
  levels>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.East.wakesSky>, same
  <verbatim|Boats.lean>>|<cell|The source recursively applies
  <verbatim|boatsSky> with threshold equal to the previous selected scale. It
  obtains a strictly increasing index map, strict decrease of selected
  scales, and finite chart levels tending to infinity. The manuscript proves
  the scalar recursion explicitly.>>|<row|<cell|Bounded lifts and their
  ultrafilter limits>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Next.UVStress.harvestedSky>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Prom/Zoom/Pepper.lean>;
  <verbatim|YM.Next.UVStress.finite_extract>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/UV_STRESS/Extract.lean>;
  <verbatim|YM.Next.UVStress.Station.Admissible>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/UV_STRESS/Station.lean>>|<cell|At each fixed cutoff,
  the lift space is a finite product of finite-dimensional spaces.
  <verbatim|lift_bound> bounds the maps on the <verbatim|F.late> set; because
  the fixed ultrafilter is below <verbatim|F.fuse>, it has a compactly
  supported image closure and hence a limit. The manuscript gives this
  finite-dimensional compactness argument.>>|<row|<cell|Exact finite-level
  symmetries, units, and short-test error>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Next.UVStress.harvestedSky>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Prom/Zoom/Pepper.lean>;
  <verbatim|YM.Next.UVStress.Station.Admissible>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/UV_STRESS/Station.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|lift_real>
  and <verbatim|lift_signed> pass to the limit by continuity. Exact units are
  inherited from the chart's unit receipt. <verbatim|short> bounds the
  finite-volume tested discrepancy by <verbatim|\<varepsilon\> \<times\>
  charge \<times\> sup(test)>; calibrated smearing and the dilation change of
  variables pass this bound to the ultrafilter limit. The selected cutoff-(k)
  vanes use <verbatim|\<varepsilon\>=costHint(k)=1/(k+1)>, while the support
  window expands with <verbatim|k>.>>|<row|<cell|Approach in tested
  correlations and injectivity>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Next.UVStress.Approaches>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/UV_STRESS/Rates.lean>;
  <verbatim|YM.Next.UVStress.MeterTest.detects>, <verbatim|.injects>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/UV_STRESS/Invert.lean>>|<cell|Finite tests separate
  grade fields by test-function uniqueness; finite-dimensionality gives a
  finite separating family. The rescaled tested functionals converge by the
  approach bound. Openness of injectivity for the resulting
  finite-dimensional map implies the chart projection is injective
  eventually. The manuscript supplies the lower-bound-on-unit-sphere
  proof.>>|<row|<cell|Corrected lifts, balanced inclusions, and eventual
  grade isomorphisms>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Next.UVStress.signed_section>,
  <verbatim|.corrected>, <verbatim|.solid>, <verbatim|.balanced>,
  <verbatim|.adjusts>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/UV_STRESS/Arrange.lean>;
  <verbatim|YM.Next.UVStress.Stations.equivalences>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/UV_STRESS/Invert.lean>;
  <verbatim|YM.Next.UVStress.DimAbove>, <verbatim|.cap_given>, same
  <verbatim|Invert.lean>; <verbatim|YM.Next.UVStress.Station.harvested>,
  <verbatim|YM.Next.UVStress.Stations.build_curve>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/UV_STRESS/Station.lean> and its immediate
  construction dependencies>|<cell|The manuscript now writes out the
  retraction-and-correction recursion and proves the balanced identity by
  direct composition and transitivity. It also explains the finite-slot
  argument transferring qualitative tested convergence. The source order is
  station extraction/projection, curve assembly, correction in selected table
  fields, then tested injectivity plus the dimension bound to choose eventual
  linear equivalences; exact balanced identities yield pairwise eventual
  inclusion compatibility. The same source <verbatim|Stations.equivalences>
  concludes <verbatim|Approaches> and <verbatim|Stable>. Funding for the
  station receipts and full-gallery inputs remains open in this
  unit.>>|<row|<cell|Full gallery and its public selected-run
  application>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Over.Gallery> and <verbatim|.gang>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Chart/Line.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|gang>
  fixes the ultrafilter and growth height, uses the reference Ward tensor,
  invokes the selected-sequence scaling producer for each positive null
  sequence, and obtains the field array by the tower construction. Its
  <verbatim|FiresSky> premise is supplied by the selected run. The
  conditional chart argument now includes the corrected-lift route and
  pairwise eventual inclusion identities. The public <verbatim|Gallery>
  application still depends on the finite-volume and scale-dependent
  receipts, including the selected run's <verbatim|FiresSky>
  input.>>|<row|<cell|Selected actual public
  caller>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Independent.constructionRun>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Independent/ConstructionRun.lean>;
  <verbatim|YM.Integration.NativePreselectedPostnumericPeriodClock.allFactorWithTreasuryPeriod_preselected_quote_orders_postnumeric_of_prediction>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/NativePreselectedPostnumericPeriodClock.lean>;
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.R2I.RG05Joint.plentifulWithPrediction>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/RG05Preconstruction/Bardo.lean>>|<cell|The
  public caller selects the run with the native postnumeric period-clock
  construction; its actual selected supplier is
  <verbatim|RG05Joint.plentifulWithPrediction>. That theorem receives the
  finite-volume receipts and calls <verbatim|YM.Trace.Over.gang>. This is the
  selected route, not a neighboring campaign theorem.>>>>>

  <section|Reorganized arguments and explicit remaining
  input><label|reorganized-arguments-and-explicit-remaining-input>

  The finite-dimensional rank-nullity step, stable-inverse estimate,
  weighted-flux coefficient extraction, two-scale normalized/trace limit,
  one-dimensional scalar normalization, strict-subsequence recursion, compact
  ultrafilter limit, finite-dimensional chart gluing, and corrected-lift
  recursion are reorganized proofs in the manuscript, not literal Lean
  theorem statements. The source producer chain supplies the identities and
  estimates listed above. In particular, the source has a weighted flux limit
  only for the two correction directions; the uncorrected term has an
  unweighted limit. The argument uses the independent uniform coefficient
  bound to multiply the former limits, and does not multiply the latter by
  the scale weight.

  The weighted-price receiver is a newly reorganized proof of the mechanism
  in <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.expenses>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Delta.lean>; its application in
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.springs> is conditional on the two weighted
  medium estimates. Its public supplier is <verbatim|YM.Trace.Over.rungs>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Slate/Garnet.lean>, which combines
  <verbatim|aspiring> and <verbatim|legacy>; the latter passes through
  <verbatim|hullage> and <verbatim|small_means>. Other remaining analytic
  inputs are (i) the scale-dependent two-direction comparison limits and
  stable inversion inputs; (ii) base/correction beam convergence and washout
  estimates; (iii) unweighted base Ward-flux limit and
  <verbatim|taxA>-weighted false/true correction flux estimates; (iv)
  separated-jet comparison and physical/reference flux limits; and (v) the
  selected-run <verbatim|FiresSky> family, finite-volume chart transport,
  lift bound, unit/covariance, arity-capped short-test bound, and dimension
  receipts. The source route is recorded above to connect these estimates to
  their suppliers. The rewritten scalar and finite-dimensional arguments are
  proved here, but these analytic estimates have not all been rederived. The
  main gallery theorem is consequently a conditional assembly.

  <section|Commands and verification record><label|commands-and-verification-record>

  Read-only inspection used <verbatim|rg -n> and <verbatim|sed -n> on the
  exact files listed above, plus <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Chart/{Masts,Laurel,Stage,North,Time,Line,Token,Dray,Limits}.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Prom/Zoom/{Boats,Running,Mast,Pepper}.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Shelves/{Lore,Route,Sapphire}.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/UV_STRESS/{Station,Rates,Arrange,Invert,Weak,Vary}.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/UV_STRESS/Dimension.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Push/STRESS_FLUX/{FreeTests,Lift,Counts,Line,Conserved}.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Further/PHYSICAL_PERIOD_LIMIT_F933/FreeRanks.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/{Lease,Delta,Prism,Rivers}.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Slate/{Garnet,Limit,Phantom,Spite}.lean>,
  and <verbatim|source/upstream.json>. The actual selected public route was
  checked through <verbatim|Lean/YM/Independent/ConstructionRun.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/RG05Preconstruction/Bardo.lean>, and
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/NativePreselectedPostnumericPeriodClock.lean>.
  <verbatim|python3 scripts/check_blueprint.py> was run and failed because
  the coordinator-owned <verbatim|blueprint/units/YM-000026/unit.json> is
  absent in this clone. No Lean or LaTeX build was run; no Lean source files
  were changed.

